04536207,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.20512193472186813,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.07439,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":49.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ServiceTitan, Inc. provides an end-to-end cloud-based software platform in the United States, Armenia, and Canada. Its platform connects and manages a range of business workflows, such as advertising, job scheduling and management, dispatching, generating estimates and invoices, payment processing and others. The company offers ServiceTitan, a platform for contractors; FieldRoutes, pest control software; and Aspire, a business management software that offers real-time reports, precise data, accurate job costing for the landscape and clean industries. In addition, the company offers FinTech products that include payment processing and third-party financing solutions. It serves HVAC, plumbing, electrical, garage door, chimney sweep, roofing, irrigation, water treatment, septic, painting, pool service, landscape, lawn care, pest control, air duct cleaning, commercial food equipment, audio visual, alarm, appliance repair, residential remodeling, locksmith, refrigeration, handyman, gutter, siding, dock and door, fire and life safety industries. The company was formerly known as Linxlogic, Inc. and changed its name to ServiceTitan, Inc. in June 2014. The company was incorporated in 2007 and is based in Glendale, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ara  Mahdessian | Co-Founder, Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 39 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $281K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $58K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["ServiceTitan, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $7.9B market cap on $961M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +12.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -18% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 68% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $105M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -15.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -23.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 21% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 7.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 400% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.9991359664783537},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 25% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $31.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (49% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 757% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ServiceTitan (NASDAQ:TTAN) CEO Ara Mahdessian Sells 63,927 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/servicetitan-nasdaqttan